    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d409-a3">

                <pb facs="0636" n="540" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg540"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 3.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Biddle to Mr. Baxter.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">San
                                Salvador</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-26"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 26,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit to you
                    herewith, for your information, a copy of a note dated the 25th instant,
                    received by me from the minister of foreign relations of Salvador, relative to
                    alleged violations of the neutrality of the interoceanic railway in Honduras by
                    the partisans of General Medina.</p>
                <p>I have communicated with the Department of State upon the subject, and now
                    present it to your attention, although the unfinished condition of the road
                    seems to absolve the United States from responsibility under the guarantee of
                    1864.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOS. BIDDLE.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
